hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15978","Waki' narrated to us, from Amr ibn Hassan, meaning al-Musalli, he said, al-Mughira ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from his father, he said: I entered the mosque of Kufa when its mosque was first built, while it was among the owners of dates that day and its walls were of soft clay, and a man was narrating to people. He said: It reached me that the Farewell Hajj of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come, so I followed a riding camel of my camels, then went out until I sat for him on the road of Arafa, or stood for him on the road of Arafa. He said: And there was a caravan, and I recognized the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them by description. A man before him said: Make way for the caravan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to him, how strange, what is with him? So I drew near him until the heads of the two she-camels differed. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that admits me to Paradise and saves me from the Fire. He said: Splendid, splendid; if you fell short in the address, you have been eloquent in the question. Understand then: Worship Allah the Mighty and Majestic, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj of the House, fast Ramadan. Make way for the caravan."
"15979","Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus, he said: I heard this hadith from al-Mughira ibn Abd Allah from his father, the like of it."
"15980","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Mughira, from his father, he said: I came upon a man narrating to people, so I sat. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was described to me while I was at Mina going to Arafat, then he mentioned the hadith. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that brings me near Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: Establish prayer, give zakat, perform Hajj of the House, fast Ramadan, love for people what you love to be given to you, and dislike for them what you dislike to be given to you. Make way for the caravan."
